---
.title = "JavaScript",
.description = "Use Yuku from JavaScript and TypeScript with the yuku package.",
.author = "Arshad Yaseen",
.date = @date("2026-10-29T00:00:00"),
.layout = "page.shtml",
---
The `yuku` package parses, analyzes, walks, builds, and prints JavaScript and TypeScript, with no third-party dependencies. It runs natively where its addon for the platform installs, and as WebAssembly everywhere else.

```bash
npm install yuku
```

Cloudflare Workers and Vercel Edge run WebAssembly only from a file, so there also install `@yuku-toolchain/wasm`.

```js
import { b, parse, print, walk } from "yuku";

const file = parse(`
  const RATE = 0.2;
  export const tax = (price: number) => price * RATE;
  export const scale = (RATE: number) => RATE * 2;
`, { path: "tax.ts", analyze: true });

const rate = file.rootScope.find("RATE");

walk(file.program, {
  Identifier(node, ctx) {
    if (file.referenceOf(node)?.binding === rate) ctx.replace(b.Literal({ value: 0.2 }));
  },
});

print(file, { strip: true }).code;
// const RATE = 0.2;
// export const tax = (price) => price * 0.2;
// export const scale = (RATE) => RATE * 2;
```
